{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-4-9","kind":"proposition","title":"为给定正方形作外接圆","englishTitle":"About a given square to circumscribe a circle.","book":4,"number":9,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":9,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":"https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷四"}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","contentId":"euclid-4-9","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7b410bf1c1b261d6e0e581a9a25500a8ddd4093cd8820313ac2c69272102704a","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-4-9.statement","euclid-4-9.construction.1","euclid-4-9.construction.2","euclid-4-9.proof.1","euclid-4-9.proof.2","euclid-4-9.proof.3","euclid-4-9.proof.4","euclid-4-9.proof.5","euclid-4-9.proof.6","euclid-4-9.proof.7","euclid-4-9.construction.3","euclid-4-9.conclusion","euclid-4-9.historical.1","euclid-4-9.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-4-9.statement","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c14c6874682a9128a9c4b24d7b7ca6446c2a95c2ff95e8a9aa97bd9671cee60d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"About a given square to circumscribe a circle."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"大约正方形个用来环绕圆圈"},{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"直角方形求作形外切圜"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"正方形求作形外切圆"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"001152037af9a71d53e9184b92e750e5247023d14deb395114b5403ac84ed5fc","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let ABCD be the given square; thus it is required to circumscribe a circle about the square ABCD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让ABCD成为给的正方形;因此,它必须限定一个大约正方形 ABCD的圆圈。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"18b46c92dedc2f4f9fdddc9cfee37a13366ff4c61aae547a955a9a89fddf35f5","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let AC, BD be joined, and let them cut one another at E."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AC,BD连接, 让它们在E之间切开。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b6f2e1cc690a58dc23f9147bdc7a248b08e85241c4a3d92b7b30e8ed67ee6adc","citations":["euclid-1-8"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Then, since DA is equal to AB, and AC is common, therefore the two sides DA, AC are equal to the two sides BA, AC; and the base DC is equal to the base BC; therefore the angle DAC is equal to the angle BAC. [[I. 8](/principles/euclid-1-8)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"DA等于AB,AC是共同的,因此,双方DA,AC等于BA,AC;底边,DC等于底边,BC;因此,角度DAC等于角度BAC。 [[I. 8](/principles/euclid-1-8)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1a0220a9015f5e52de05281221a15480f2f32cc4133ef9c6dee3a8e2f2c5dc88","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the angle DAB is bisected by AC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,DAB角被AC角分了两部分。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6e23f8f1fc7f495d4a8c82ed4307a823561f7a3a948a399c95d8787797cd8ab0","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that each of the angles ABC, BCD, CDA is bisected by the straight lines AC, DB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明,ABC、BCD、CDA角的每一个角都被AC、DB直线分开。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"28d3f647edd71171dc2cfeb7a1f94560a2881eba15f2e62fc2d6061d3a5bb0d8","citations":["euclid-1-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since the angle DAB is equal to the angle ABC, and the angle EAB is half the angle DAB, and the angle EBA half the angle ABC, therefore the angle EAB is also equal to the angle EBA; so that the side EA is also equal to EB. [[I. 6](/principles/euclid-1-6)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,DAB角等于ABC角,EAB角等于DAB角的一半,ABC角等于ABC角的一半,因此,EAB角也等于EBA角;因此,EA角也等于EB角。 [[I. 6](/principles/euclid-1-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3efb01ad3332d46579a9abeb98be72abcc5298d7b236ab823f0a4e18d6a47ecc","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines EA, EB is equal to each of the straight lines EC, ED."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明,EA、EB直线中的每一条直线都等于EC、ED直线中的每一条直线。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"73f7e79cec3f6644f5aab4d8425150606226b98dc083ee66498fe9b5f51361e1","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the four straight lines EA, EB, EC, ED are equal to one another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,四条直线EA、EB、EC、ED等同。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"fa242f2dc959a55c6256db932f17afeb2ac2376b4b248a2006ff49ec04a2177e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the circle described with centre E and distance one of the straight lines EA, EB, EC, ED will pass also through the remaining points; and it will have been circumscribed about the square ABCD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,以E中心为主的圆圈和EA、EB、EC、ED直线之一的距离也将穿过其余的点;它大约为正方形 ABCD。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.construction.3","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":10,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f60c5ce21b1f9a9314b9ae42e196a511a61888666dd1984a92e20d39d34ba6a5","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let it be circumscribed, as ABCD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它被限定为ABCD"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":11,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"006c0f781dc9ef2e2353a637f81a14bb5d67c101574ceec9dd70cffcf9a27aed","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore about the given square a circle has been circumscribed. Q. E. F."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,对给定的正方形个圆圈作了限定。"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.historical.1","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":12,"kind":"historical_note","title":"徐光启、利玛窦历史中译 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"01a2721aa3334ff4680c45156ef34f9d8e6b622832a3f1dd8e9269c880f6a076","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"直角方形求作形外切圜法曰甲乙丙丁直角方形求作外切圜先作对角两线为甲丙乙丁而交于戊其甲乙丁角形之甲乙甲丁两腰等即甲乙丁甲丁乙两角亦等〈一卷五〉而乙甲丁为直角即甲乙丁甲丁乙俱半直角〈一卷卅二〉依显丙乙丁丙丁乙亦俱半直角而四角俱等又戊甲丁戊丁甲两角等即戊甲戊丁两边亦等〈一卷六〉依显戊甲戊乙两边亦等而戊乙戊丙两边戊丙戊丁两边各等次作圜以戊为心甲为界必过乙丙丁而为形外切圜"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"正方形求作形外切圆作图方法如下：甲乙丙丁正方形求作外切圆先作对角两线为甲丙乙丁而交于戊其甲乙丁三角形之甲乙甲丁两腰等即甲乙丁甲丁乙两角亦等〈一卷五〉而乙甲丁为直角即甲乙丁甲丁乙都半直角〈一卷卅二〉依显丙乙丁丙丁乙亦都半直角而四角都等又戊甲丁戊丁甲两角等即戊甲戊丁两边亦等〈一卷六〉依显戊甲戊乙两边亦等而戊乙戊丙两边戊丙戊丁两边各等次作圆以戊为心甲为界必过乙丙丁而为形外切圆"}]},{"id":"euclid-4-9.source","contentId":"euclid-4-9","revisionId":"euclid-4-9@raw-7b410bf1c1b261d6","order":13,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1fc49597696dbf474a3ab3f7a203bedd3f1c7b6fd527a57789c123c38e84858c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\nHistorical Chinese source: https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷四"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-4-9:euclid-1-8:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-4-9","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-4-9.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-1-8","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9/","sourceLabel":"I. 8"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-4-9:euclid-1-6:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-4-9","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-4-9.proof.4"],"targetContentId":"euclid-1-6","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:4.prop.9/","sourceLabel":"I. 6"}}],"incomingEdges":[],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-4-9:euclid-1-8:explicit","id":"euclid-1-8","book":1,"number":8,"kind":"proposition","title":"三角形全等：三边分别相等","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"},{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-4-9:euclid-1-6:explicit","id":"euclid-1-6","book":1,"number":6,"kind":"proposition","title":"等腰三角形逆定理：等角对等边","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-polygon","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
